<header><h1>The Deepwrought Scholarate: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/F_deepwrought">The Deepwrought Scholarate</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2 id="research-team"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Deepwrought_Scholarate#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Research%20Team">Research Team</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li><sc>Research Team</sc> may be used both when the Deepwrought player commits ground forces to a planet another player controls and when another player commits ground forces to a planet the Deepwrought player controls.<sup>9</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>9</sup> Designer Q&amp;A, &ldquo;Research Team Offensive Use&rdquo;: &ldquo;Deepwrought may use their Research Teams ability whether they are committing ground forces on a planet another player controls or if another player is committing ground forces on a planet they control.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Deepwrought player uses <sc>Research Team</sc> when another player commits ground forces to a planet they control, the invading player cannot engage in ground combat with the Deepwrought player on that planet during the same activation in which the Deepwrought player enters coexistence.<sup>9</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>9</sup> Same answer: &ldquo;If Deepwrought uses their ability defensively, the invading player may not engage in ground combat with the Deepwrought on the same activation that Deepwrought enters coexistence.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Deepwrought player uses <sc>Research Team</sc> when another player commits ground forces to a planet the Deepwrought player controls, the ground combat is skipped and the invading player gains control of the planet during the <b>Establish Control</b> step. If another player was already coexisting on that planet, the invading player may instead choose to end that player&rsquo;s coexistence, resolving a ground combat against them; the winner gains control during the <b>Establish Control</b> step.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;When DWS uses research teams to coexist, this occurs during the commit ground forces step, so when you get to the ground combat step you skip it, moving straight to the Establish Control step, where you gain control. If there were another player coexisting on that planet before invasion, though, you may choose to end that player&rsquo;s coexistence.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="oceanbound"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Deepwrought_Scholarate#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Oceanbound">Oceanbound</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Ocean cards are spent as though they were planet cards. However, oceans are not planets, and do not count as planets for the purpose of scoring objectives, such as <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Objectives#Prophecy_of_Kings_Expansion:~:text=Push%20Boundaries"><i>Push Boundaries</i></a>.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;What are the Ocean cards exactly? Do they count as planets for scoring purposes (i.e. Push Boundaries)? &hellip; A: Oceans do not count as planets for scoring. They may be spent as planet cards.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol><li>When the Deepwrought player scores objectives, planets they are <a href="/R_coexistence">coexisting</a> on do count as planets they control. This is a function of coexistence, not of oceans, and other players do not count those planets as controlled by the Deepwrought player.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;If DWS is coexisting on 3 planets and has 3 they control, they count as 6 when scoring Push Boundaries. How many do they control when other players want to score Push Boundaries? A: Control via coexistence is only seen by the player coexisting, so the other players see 3 planets controlled.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li></ol>
    <li>If all of the Deepwrought player&rsquo;s ocean cards are already in play, they cannot resolve <sc>Oceanbound</sc> to ready one of their oceans.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Oceanbound (Ability): If the Deepwrought player has all their oceans out, can they still resolve Oceanbound &hellip; so as to ready one of their oceans? A: No&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Ocean cards are readied at the end of the agenda phase, like planets.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found. Owner ruling (2026-11-21): planets, including oceans, space stations and The Triad, are readied at the end of the agenda phase.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Attachments such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Relics#Codex_II:~:text=Nano-Forge"><i>Nano&ndash;Forge</i></a> relic and the <a href="/F_ul">Ul</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Titans_of_Ul#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Terraform"><i>Terraform</i></a> promissory note cannot be attached to an ocean card.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Can Nano-Forge and/or Terraform be attached to an Ocean Card? A: No, they are oceans&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="share-knowledge"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Deepwrought_Scholarate#Faction_Promissory_Note:~:text=Share%20Knowledge">Share Knowledge</a> <sub>(Promissory Note)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If a player gains the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Antimass_Deflectors"><i>Antimass Deflectors</i></a> technology through <i>Share Knowledge</i> and later loses it, their units may remain in and move out of any asteroid fields they are currently in, but cannot move additional units into or through.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;If I lose Antimass Deflectors while my ships sit in an asteroid field, or place units in an anomaly, what happens?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Nothing &mdash; anomaly rules restrict moving into or through them, not being in them or moving out. Ships already there stay and may leave normally&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Deepwrought player is eliminated, <i>Share Knowledge</i> and its technology remain in play until the status phase, when the promissory note is returned to the game box.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;What happens to a technology gained via the Deepwrought Scholarate PN, Share Knowledge, if the DWS player is eliminated? &hellip; A: The DWS PN remains in play with the technology until status at which point the PN is returned to the box.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="hydrothermal-mining"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Deepwrought_Scholarate#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Hydrothermal%20Mining">Hydrothermal Mining</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    </ol>

<h2 id="radical-advancement"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Deepwrought_Scholarate#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Radical%20Advancement">Radical Advancement</a> <sub>(Technology)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If the Deepwrought player replaces the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Antimass_Deflectors"><i>Antimass Deflectors</i></a> technology, their units may remain in and move out of any asteroid fields they are currently in, but cannot move additional units into or through.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;If I lose Antimass Deflectors while my ships sit in an asteroid field, or place units in an anomaly, what happens?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Nothing &mdash; anomaly rules restrict moving into or through them, not being in them or moving out. Ships already there stay and may leave normally&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Deepwrought player may replace <i>Radical Advancement</i> itself for a biotic technology with two prerequisites.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the Deepwrought player has the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Alliance"><i>Alliance</i></a> promissory note in their play area, they will not draw an action card from the ability of the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Leaders:~:text=Nekro%20Acidos">Nekro Acidos</a> commander when they resolve <i>Radical Advancement</i>.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="d-w-s-luminous"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Deepwrought_Scholarate#Flagship:~:text=D.W.S.%20Luminous">D.W.S. Luminous</a> <sub>(Flagship)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The <i>D.W.S. Luminous</i> gains +1 for each system it moves through that contains the Deepwrought player&rsquo;s units, regardless of any other units present.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;D.W.S. Luminous (Flagship): Does it gain +1 for only your units or does it require both &hellip;? A: It gains +1 for each system if it moves through that contains your units, regardless of any other units present.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The <a href="/F_argent">Argent</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Argent_Flight#Faction_Technologies:~:text=Aerie%20Hololattice"><i>Aerie Hololattice</i></a> technology prevents the <i>D.W.S. Luminous</i> from moving through systems containing the <a href="/F_argent">Argent</a> player&rsquo;s structures.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;D.W.S. Luminous (Flagship): How does this interact with Aerie Hololattice? &hellip; A: Aerie Hololattice stops it moving through.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="doctor-carrina"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Deepwrought_Scholarate#Leaders:~:text=Doctor%20Carrina">Doctor Carrina</a> <sub>(Agent)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Doctor Carrina may be used even if no prerequisite is skipped, but the coexisting infantry is not placed. This includes when the player chooses not to ignore any prerequisites, or researches a technology with no prerequisites. The player may ignore prerequisites they already fulfill on a technology that has at least one prerequisite.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;The agent may be used, but the coexisting infantry is not placed if a prerequisite was not skipped &hellip; The receiving player may still ignore prerequisites even if they already fulfill them on a technology that has at least 1 prerequisite.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>The Deepwrought player cannot use Doctor Carrina to start coexisting with the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player, as the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player cannot skip a prerequisite.<sup>6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Is it possible &hellip; for the Deepwrought player to start coexisting with the Nekro player by using Doctor Carrina? A: No, there is no way for Nekro to fulfill the &lsquo;they do skip a prerequisite&rsquo;&rdquo; condition.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="aello"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Deepwrought_Scholarate#Leaders:~:text=Aello">Aello</a> <sub>(Commander)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The Deepwrought player does not have the capability to prevent other players from using the ability of Aello.<sup>2,7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can a researching player use both the Deepwrought commander and alliance for -2?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; each is a separate optional trigger, and the Deepwrought and their ally can&rsquo;t refuse.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook, Aello (Deepwrought Commander): &ldquo;The Deepwrought player cannot choose to disallow Aello from being used by other players.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Aello can only reduce a cost paid with <a href="/R_resources">resources</a>, including <a href="/R_trade_goods">trade goods</a> spent in place of resources. It cannot reduce a cost paid with influence, trade goods spent in place of influence, or any other currency.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a player has the Deepwrought player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Alliance"><i>Alliance</i></a> promissory note, then other players may use the ability of either or both (or neither):<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can a researching player use both the Deepwrought commander and alliance for -2?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; each is a separate optional trigger, and the Deepwrought and their ally can&rsquo;t refuse.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <ol>
        <li>Another player may use the ability from both for a two resource discount, triggering the commodity ability for both the Deepwrought player and the player with their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Alliance"><i>Alliance</i></a> promissory note.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can a researching player use both the Deepwrought commander and alliance for -2?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes &mdash; each is a separate optional trigger, and the Deepwrought and their ally can&rsquo;t refuse.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>Another player may use the ability from only the Deepwrought player for a one resource discount, triggering the commodity ability for just the Deepwrought player.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> Same entry: &ldquo;each is a separate optional trigger.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>Another player may use the ability from only the player with the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Alliance"><i>Alliance</i></a> promissory note for a one resource discount, triggering the commodity ability for just the player with the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Alliance"><i>Alliance</i></a> promissory note.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> Same entry: &ldquo;each is a separate optional trigger.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>Another player may use the ability from neither player, and receive no discount; the commodity ability will trigger for neither the Deepwrought player nor the player with their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Alliance"><i>Alliance</i></a> promissory note.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> Same entry: &ldquo;each is a separate optional trigger.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>The Deepwrought player and the player with their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Alliance"><i>Alliance</i></a> promissory note may each use the ability of the other for a one resource discount, triggering the commodity ability for that other player.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
        <li>If the <a href="/F_mahact">Mahact</a> player has the Deepwrought player&rsquo;s command token in their fleet pool, then this gives each other player the option of another discount. The Deepwrought player, the player with their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Promissory_Notes#Alliance"><i>Alliance</i></a> promissory note, and the <a href="/F_mahact">Mahact</a> player may choose up to two of the other players with the ability, triggering their commodity ability, and resulting in a corresponding discount of up to two resources. All other players may choose up to three of the players with the ability, triggering their commodity ability, and resulting in a corresponding discount of up to three resources.<sup>*</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Unverified</b>: No source found.</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="ta-zern"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Deepwrought_Scholarate#Leaders:~:text=Ta%20Zern">Ta Zern</a> &mdash; <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Deepwrought_Scholarate#Leaders:~:text=Wave%20Function%20Collapse">Wave Function Collapse</a> <sub>(Hero)</sub></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If they also owned the purged technology, the Deepwrought player too will research another technology.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;If Wave Function Collapse purges a technology another player gained through Share Knowledge &hellip;?&rdquo;: &ldquo;the holder owns the gained technology, so it is purged and they research another.&rdquo; Covers a different holder.</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If another player has gained the purged technology through <i>Share Knowledge</i>, they own it, so they purge it and research another technology, which they keep after <i>Share Knowledge</i> is returned.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;If Wave Function Collapse purges a technology another player gained through Share Knowledge, does that player research a replacement?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Most players say yes: the holder owns the gained technology, so it is purged and they research another, keeping it after the note returns.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player purges a technology, they will gain three command tokens instead of researching another technology.<sup>2</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Implicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Can the Nekro Virus play Reveal Prototype?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Yes, gaining 3 command tokens instead of the technology.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>

